    <!--
      HOW TO ADD A NEW RELEASE:
      1. Bump MARKETING_VERSION and CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION in Xcode.
      2. Export Lotion.app to ~/Downloads (or pass -build to archive,
         notarize and staple it automatically).
      3. Run: go run ./cmd/lotion-release
         - Enter release notes when prompted, or run non-interactively with
           flags, e.g.:
             go run ./cmd/lotion-release -yes \
               -notes "Faster search
             Fixed table editing"
           (-notes-file <path> reads bullets from a file instead.)

      The release tool creates Lotion.dmg, signs it with Sparkle, prepends
      this appcast, commits/pushes appcast.xml to main, and creates the GitHub
      release with the DMG attached.

      Newest release goes on top.
    -->

    <item>
      <title>Version 0.0.4</title>
      <sparkle:version>4</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.0.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:14:07 +0000</pubDate>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <h2>What's New in 0.0.4</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Lotion now has a built-in MCP server, so AI agents like Claude Code and Codex can read, search, write and organize your notes, add attachments, use the scratchpad, change settings, and publish notes to your Lotion Share worker.</li>
          <li>Set it up in Settings → AI Agents: copy the command for your agent and run it once in a terminal.</li>
          <li>Pressing Tab in a table now clears the cell selection as it moves to the next cell.</li>
        </ul>
      ]]></description>
